{{safesubst:unexpected|desc=
* The {{tip|slow}}, {{as|'''bonus''' physical damage}} to champions, and keg {{as|health}} decay speed are determined when the keg is placed.
** The keg {{as|health}} decay timer indicator is instead based on '''Gangplank's''' current level, which can lead to desynchronization. [https://www.youtube.com/shorts/3rYb4Ujs17U] {{bug}}|affectedEffects=Gangplank E|estimatedPatchOrigin=V5.14|<!--added automatically-->wikiUploadTimestamp=1774027850|<!--added automatically-->pagename=Template:Data Gangplank/Powder Keg
}}<!--Decay timer desynchronization bug-->
* The triggering attack's damage can include {{ais|Parrrley|Gangplank}} base damage and {{tip|Spellblade}}.
* The percentage armor penetration stacks multiplicatively with other sources of percentage armor penetration.
* When triggered with critical strike, ''Spellblade'' and the bonus damage to champions are added after the calculations.
* [[Damage modifier]]s are applied to the damage dealt '''by''' kegs, but not to the damage dealt '''to''' kegs.
<!--hexoptics didnt proc on kegs even before they fixed this-->
* The total damage can be calculated with this formula:<br>{aDMG * [2 ({{ii|Infinity Edge|+ 0.30}})]} + sDMG + cDMG<br>Where:
** aDMG = Triggering attack's damage
** sDMG = Spellblade's damage
** cDMG = Bonus damage to champions
* Kegs have special interactions with {{tip|Spellblade}}:
** If the keg destroying attack was empowered with ''Spellblade'', its damage will be added to the explosions' damage.
** If the keg was not destroyed, it will consume the effect and the keg will store the damage it would have dealt. If the storing keg is the initial detonation of the chain, it will add its damage to the explosions' damage as if it was triggered with ''Spellblade''.
** If the storing keg was attacked with a new instance of ''Spellblade'', it will override the previously stored damage (if different).
** Damage can only be stored if ''Spellblade'' was consumed by '''Gangplank'''.
** The stored damage is static and will not change if '''Gangplank's''' '''base''' attack damage or ability power (see below) changes. 
* Specific {{tip|Spellblade}} item interactions:
** {{ii|Bloodsong}}: Dealing damage with kegs to champions won't apply ''Expose Weakness'' to them.
** {{ii|Iceborn Gauntlet}}: The frost field will be created on the location of the keg that is attacked.
** {{ii|Lich Bane}}: The {{as|magic damage}} will be added to the explosions' damage, but will be dealt as {{as|physical damage}}.
** {{ii|Trinity Force}}: Attacking kegs grants the movespeed from {{nie|Quicken}}; dealing damage with the explosion does not since it does not trigger {{tip|on-hit}} effects.
* Kegs triggering a chain reaction will show a lit fuse traveling toward other kegs.
** The lit fuse is only visual and does not affect the time it takes for kegs to explode.
* Placed kegs do '''not''' grant {{tip|sight|vision}} until they explode, but they are revealed to '''Gangplank'''.
** If '''Gangplank''' loses allied vision, for instance due to {{tip|nearsight}}, he will also lose vision on his kegs temporarily.
** Kegs prematurely grant {{tip|sight}} of their explosion radius (including across terrain and into bushes) if {{ai|Parrrley|Gangplank}} or a lit fuse is traveling towards them.
*** This area reveal happens even if {{ai|Parrrley|Gangplank}} is not going to make it explode.
* An exploding ''Powder Keg'' will splash {{ais|Parrrley|Gangplank}} '''bonus''' damage, and will also be modified if the attack {{tip|critical strike|critically strikes}}.
* Attacks against ''Powder Kegs'' will apply {{tip|on-hit}} effects (such as {{iis|Tiamat}} {{nie|Cleave}}), but {{tip|proc damage}} against the keg itself is reduced to 0.
** Damage from [[on-hit]] effects will therefore '''not''' increase the damage of the explosion.
** {{tip|Spellblade}} is a {{tt|special-cased exception|Since late Season 9 - previously, Spellblade worked simply because it would add to the attack's damage directly}}.
* ''Powder Kegs'' will take damage from effects that apply on-hit effects (eg. {{iis|Guinsoo's Rageblade}} {{nie|Seething Strike}} <!--d&d-->), but will remain at {{as|1 health}} if they would be killed by them.
* The number of ''Powder Kegs'' in stock is visible under '''Gangplank's''' [[health bar]] for all players.
* '''Gangplank''' stocks ''Powder Kegs'' even if the ability hasn't been learned yet.
** This is due to the recharge rate at level 1 being set the same as level 0.
** While at maximum charges, ranking up the ability to rank 3 or 5 grants the remaining charge immediately regardless of the recharge timer.
* If a keg is destroyed during the {{rutngt|0.3}}-delay between explosions, '''Gangplank''' will plunder {{g|gold}} and ''{{ai|Silver Serpents|Gangplank}}'' upon killing enemies as if he had done so using {{ai|Parrrley|Gangplank}}.{{bug|1}}
** This effect persists through {{tip|death}} and will only end upon killing an enemy with {{ai|Parrrley|Gangplank}}.
